<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herstal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herstal is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> just north of Liège, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was a residence of the Carolingian family, the home of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-of-herstal">Pepin of Herstal</a>, and from the early modern period it was a centre of arms manufacture, home since 1889 of the Fabrique Nationale (FN Herstal).</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herstal.jpg" alt="Herstal" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VilleHerstal · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vue_Herstal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
